"Simultaneously, this individual reliance mirrors an acute systemic fragility at the societal level. Modern power grids, water treatment plants, financial clearinghouses, and supply chains operate through tightly coupled digital networks vulnerable to cyberattacks, solar storms, or single-point software failures. By dismantling analog backups in the name of cost-cutting efficiency, societies have traded robust redundancy for brittle hyper-optimization.",
