"texte": [
"Dear Maya and fellow young petitioners, having presided yesterday over the constitutional hearing in which you and twenty-four youths from coastal and agricultural regions argued for the legal right to a stable climate, I felt compelled to write to you outside the formal language of judicial decrees. Listening to your testimonies—describing how salinized groundwater is ruining family orchards and how extreme heatwaves now close rural schools—reminded our bench that environmental degradation is never merely an abstract ecological statistic; it is an acute question of fundamental justice across both geography and time.",
"Environmental justice confronts us with a profound moral asymmetry. Across the globe, the communities suffering earliest and most severely from toxic pollution, rising seas, and agricultural collapse—low-income neighborhoods, Indigenous nations, and developing countries—are precisely those that contributed least to historical greenhouse gas emissions. Simultaneously, this spatial injustice is compounded by an unprecedented 'intergenerational tyranny': present political majorities and corporate boards reap immediate financial gains from ecological depletion while offloading irreversible climatic debts onto children and unborn citizens who possess neither ballots nor representation in today's legislatures.",
"For centuries, legal systems recognized duties only among living contemporaries capable of reciprocal contracts. Yet, as constitutional courts worldwide increasingly affirm, no generation holds absolute sovereign title to destroy Earth's life-support systems; rather, each generation is a temporary trustee bound by fiduciary duty to pass on an intact, habitable biosphere to its successors.",
" skeptics occasionally object that granting legal standing to youth or future generations encroaches upon parliamentary discretion. On the contrary, constitutional rights exist precisely to prevent short-term majorities from irreversibly destroying the foundational conditions of human dignity and liberty for those who follow.",
"Whatever the formal ruling our court delivers next month, Maya, know that your generation has already transformed legal consciousness. By insisting that justice extends beyond immediate self-interest to encompass vulnerable neighbors and the unborn, you are helping law evolve into a true guardian of planetary life."
