"texte": [
"At a bustling grain terminal on the Black Sea coast, dockworker Tariq Hassan watched cargo cranes stand motionless against a grey morning sky, halted by naval blockades and drifting sea mines miles offshore. Four thousand kilometers away in an East African market town, baker Amina Osei stared at wholesale flour prices that had doubled in a single month, forcing families in her neighborhood to cut back to one meal a day. Though separated by oceans and continents, Tariq and Amina were bound together by the invisible shockwaves of modern armed conflict—a stark reminder that in an deeply interdependent world, no war ever remains truly localized.",
